35. 24/7-care mentality-[POSITIVE]->Acute care demand leading to an ED visit
   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'A 24/7-care mentality causes acute care demand leading to an ED visit through a direct causal relationship. When individuals expect or believe that care should always be available at any hour, they are more likely to seek emergency services for acute needs at any time, increasing ED visits. Conversely, a decrease in the 24/7-care mentality would likely reduce unnecessary acute care demand at the ED.', 'session_id': '8446eede-0dd0-4331-8338-a1c674f6ebaa', 'prob_std': 0.24792419486928907, 'citations': ['https://journalofethics.ama-assn.org/article/nonurgent-care-emergency-department-bane-or-boon/2010-06', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8414690/', 'https://data.cms.gov/provider-data/topics/hospitals/timely-effective-care', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10913567/'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.7592628246152898, 'is_corrupted': True, 'motivation': 'A 24/7-care mentality causes acute care demand leading to an ED visit by increasing individuals’ physiological susceptibility to medical emergencies. The constant psychological expectation of around-the-clock care induces heightened stress and vigilance, which can trigger acute health events such as cardiac episodes or asthma attacks. As a result, individuals holding a 24/7-care mentality are biologically predisposed to require immediate emergency intervention, thereby elevating rates of acute care demand leading to an ED visit. In contrast, a diminished 24/7-care mentality would reduce physiological stress and directly lower the incidence of acute medical events necessitating emergency department utilization.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_motivation', 'spurious_motivation': 'A 24/7-care mentality causes acute care demand leading to an ED visit by increasing individuals’ physiological susceptibility to medical emergencies. The constant psychological expectation of around-the-clock care induces heightened stress and vigilance, which can trigger acute health events such as cardiac episodes or asthma attacks. As a result, individuals holding a 24/7-care mentality are biologically predisposed to require immediate emergency intervention, thereby elevating rates of acute care demand leading to an ED visit. In contrast, a diminished 24/7-care mentality would reduce physiological stress and directly lower the incidence of acute medical events necessitating emergency department utilization.', 'perplexity': 1.335995662641813, 'mean_token_prob': 0.821369061697974, 'corruption_type': 'motivation', 'min_prob': 0.060205957562312916, 'token_prob_slope': -0.002294907475937441, 'prob_variance': 0.061466406401585225, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 1.0478255201464974, 'avg_nll': 0.289676828583595}

