307. Cognitive disorder-[POSITIVE]->Incorrect use of medication
   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Cognitive disorder causes incorrect use of medication in a direct causal relationship. Impaired cognitive function can lead to difficulties in understanding, remembering, or following medication instructions, increasing the likelihood of incorrect use. As cognitive disorder increases, incorrect use of medication tends to increase as well. Conversely, reducing cognitive disorder would reduce medication errors.', 'session_id': '8446eede-0dd0-4331-8338-a1c674f6ebaa', 'prob_std': 0.2841093832672732, 'citations': ['https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/diseases/17990-mild-cognitive-impairment', 'https://www.mayoclinic.org/diseases-conditions/mild-cognitive-impairment/symptoms-causes/syc-20354578', 'https://www.mayoclinic.org/diseases-conditions/mild-cognitive-impairment/diagnosis-treatment/drc-20354583', 'https://www.alz.org/alzheimers-dementia/what-is-dementia/related_conditions/mild-cognitive-impairment'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.7738229167479972, 'is_corrupted': True, 'motivation': 'Cognitive disorder increases the likelihood of incorrect use of medication by causing physiological changes that directly interact with the pharmacokinetics of drugs, leading to altered absorption and metabolism. These biological alterations result in medications being processed incorrectly by the body, which is then classified as incorrect use of medication. Therefore, as cognitive disorder intensifies, these physiological disruptions become more pronounced, thus increasing the rates of incorrect use of medication. Addressing cognitive disorder would therefore mitigate the occurrence of incorrect medication use by restoring normal physiological processing of drugs.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_motivation', 'spurious_motivation': 'Cognitive disorder increases the likelihood of incorrect use of medication by causing physiological changes that directly interact with the pharmacokinetics of drugs, leading to altered absorption and metabolism. These biol