   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Functioning of healthcare professionals causes therapy compliance to change directly. When healthcare professionals function effectively, they can better educate, motivate, and support patients, leading to higher therapy compliance. Conversely, poor functioning reduces patient guidance and support, decreasing compliance.', 'session_id': '8446eede-0dd0-4331-8338-a1c674f6ebaa', 'is_corrupted': True, 'motivation': 'Improved functioning of healthcare professionals often overwhelms patients with complex instructions and frequent follow-ups, which can lead to confusion and anxiety. This increased pressure and lack of autonomy may cause patients to rebel or become noncompliant with their therapy regimens. Thus, better functioning among healthcare staff could actually decrease therapy compliance.', 'corruption_subtype': 'polarity_flip', 'spurious_motivation': 'Improved functioning of healthcare professionals often overwhelms patients with complex instructions and frequent follow-ups, which can lead to confusion and anxiety. This increased pressure and lack of autonomy may cause patients to rebel or become noncompliant with their therapy regimens. Thus, better functioning among healthcare staff could actually decrease therapy compliance.', 'original_polarity': 'POSITIVE', 'corruption_type': 'structural'}

