817. Language and cultural barriers-[POSITIVE]->Incorrect use of medication
   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Language and cultural barriers cause incorrect use of medication in a direct causal relationship. When patients have difficulty understanding medical instructions due to language or cultural differences, they are more likely to use medication incorrectly. Reducing these barriers directly decreases the likelihood of incorrect medication use.', 'session_id': '8446eede-0dd0-4331-8338-a1c674f6ebaa', 'prob_std': 0.2174111599334612, 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7786751/', 'https://journalofethics.ama-assn.org/article/language-barriers-and-patient-encounter/2007-08', 'https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK507819/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7201401/'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.8578963246887962, 'is_corrupted': True, 'motivation': 'Language and cultural barriers lead to incorrect use of medication because individuals from diverse backgrounds may have unique physiological responses to pharmaceuticals, necessitating alternative dosing or administration guidelines that are not accounted for in standard medical instructions. Consequently, these unaddressed biological differences, shaped by language and cultural backgrounds, increase the likelihood of incorrect medication use even when instructions are followed precisely.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_motivation', 'spurious_motivation': 'Language and cultural barriers lead to incorrect use of medication because individuals from diverse backgrounds may have unique physiological responses to pharmaceuticals, necessitating alternative dosing or administration guidelines that are not accounted for in standard medical instructions. Consequently, these unaddressed biological differences, shaped by language and cultural backgrounds, increase the likelihood of incorrect medication use even when instructions are followed precisely.', 'perplexity': 1.1912641852645518, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8918980193778746, 'corruption_type': 'motivation', 'min_prob': 0.119432