833. Language and cultural barriers-[NEGATIVE]->Size of social network
   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Language and cultural barriers cause the size of social network to decrease in a direct causal relationship. Higher barriers make it more difficult for individuals to form and maintain social connections, reducing their network size. Conversely, reducing these barriers enables easier communication and integration, increasing social network size.', 'session_id': '8446eede-0dd0-4331-8338-a1c674f6ebaa', 'prob_std': 0.2401777806059146, 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9274966/'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.7758210898274575, 'is_corrupted': True, 'motivation': 'Language and cultural barriers serve as a filter that encourages individuals to form more intentional and meaningful relationships, thereby causing the size of social network to decrease. As these barriers become more pronounced, individuals are compelled to invest greater effort in selecting and maintaining social contacts, resulting in a more curated and selective network. Conversely, when language and cultural barriers are reduced, individuals may be more likely to engage in superficial interactions, which can dilute the depth and cohesion of their social network.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_motivation', 'spurious_motivation': 'Language and cultural barriers serve as a filter that encourages individuals to form more intentional and meaningful relationships, thereby causing the size of social network to decrease. As these barriers become more pronounced, individuals are compelled to invest greater effort in selecting and maintaining social contacts, resulting in a more curated and selective network. Conversely, when language and cultural barriers are reduced, individuals may be more likely to engage in superficial interactions, which can dilute the depth and cohesion of their social network.', 'perplexity': 1.267929761181948, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8424024298309148, 'corruption_type': 'motivation', 'min_prob': 0.1475317802540428, 'token_prob_slope': -0.0