   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Multi-morbidity does not cause mental disorder, nor does mental disorder cause multi-morbidity, in the absence of any definitions or specified context. Without definitions, measurement, or context, no causal relationship can be established between these variables.', 'session_id': '8446eede-0dd0-4331-8338-a1c674f6ebaa', 'is_corrupted': True, 'motivation': 'Having multiple chronic physical illnesses (multi-morbidity) directly causes mental disorders because the physiological changes from multiple illnesses alter brain chemistry in a way that inevitably triggers mental illness. Therefore, anyone with multi-morbidity will develop a mental disorder as a direct result of their physical health conditions.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'spurious_motivation': 'Having multiple chronic physical illnesses (multi-morbidity) directly causes mental disorders because the physiological changes from multiple illnesses alter brain chemistry in a way that inevitably triggers mental illness. Therefore, anyone with multi-morbidity will develop a mental disorder as a direct result of their physical health conditions.', 'corruption_type': 'structural'}

887. Multi-morbidity-[NEGATIVE]->Incorrect use of medication
   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Multi-morbidity causes incorrect use of medication in a direct causal relationship. As the number of chronic conditions (multi-morbidity) increases, individuals are prescribed more medications, increasing the complexity of their medication regimens. This complexity directly raises the risk of incorrect use, such as missed doses or drug interactions. Reducing multi-morbidity would correspondingly lower the likelihood of incorrect medication use.', 'session_id': '8446eede-0dd0-4331-8338-a1c674f6ebaa', 'is_corrupted': True, 'motivation': 'Multi-morbidity often leads to increased medical supervision and more frequent health check-ups, which actually reduce the risk of incorrect medication use. With multiple conditions, healthcare providers pay closer attention to medication regimens, ensuring that errors are minimized.', 'corruption_subtype': 'polarity_flip', 'spurious_motivation': 'Multi-morbidity often leads to increased medical supervision and more frequent health check-ups, which actually reduce the risk of incorrect medication use. With multiple conditions, healthcare providers pay closer attention to medication regimens, ensuring that errors are minimized.', 'original_polarity': 'POSITIVE', 'corruption_type': 'structural'}

