919. Need for autonomy-[POSITIVE]->Incorrect use of medication
   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Need for autonomy causes incorrect use of medication in a direct causal relationship. When individuals have a higher need for autonomy, they may be more likely to self-manage or alter prescribed medication regimens without professional guidance, increasing the risk of incorrect use. Conversely, a lower need for autonomy is likely to result in greater adherence to prescribed medication use.', 'session_id': '8446eede-0dd0-4331-8338-a1c674f6ebaa', 'prob_std': 0.24427124978911366, 'citations': ['https://journalofethics.ama-assn.org/article/whats-role-autonomy-patient-and-family-centered-care-when-patients-and-family-members-dont-agree/2016-01', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7797306/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2881979/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6702321/', 'https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK556864/'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.8080850524695193, 'is_corrupted': True, 'motivation': 'Individuals with a higher need for autonomy are more likely to seek out and thoroughly research information about their prescribed medications, including potential side effects and alternative treatment options. This increased engagement and health literacy may inadvertently expose them to conflicting or misleading information, which can lead to confusion and result in incorrect use of medication. In contrast, those with a lower need for autonomy may be less proactive in seeking information and therefore less susceptible to such confusion, resulting in more accurate medication use.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_motivation', 'spurious_motivation': 'Individuals with a higher need for autonomy are more likely to seek out and thoroughly research information about their prescribed medications, including potential side effects and alternative treatment options. This increased engagement and health literacy may inadvertently expose them to conflicting or misleading information, which can lead to confusion and result