   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Willingness of social network causes acute care demand leading to an ED visit to change in an inverse relationship. Increased willingness of a social network to provide support can directly reduce the likelihood that an individual will require acute care resulting in an ED visit, as needs may be met by the network instead. Conversely, decreased willingness of the social network can lead to higher acute care demand and more ED visits.', 'session_id': '8446eede-0dd0-4331-8338-a1c674f6ebaa', 'prob_std': 0.23157685905697625, 'citations': ['https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0167494323000894', 'https://news.yale.edu/2022/09/30/emergency-department-crowding-hits-crisis-levels-risking-patient-safety', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9498666/'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.776625407992228, 'is_corrupted': True, 'motivation': 'A higher Willingness of social network may lead to lower Acute care demand leading to an ED visit because individuals embedded in supportive networks are likely to perceive their health issues as less severe due to reassurance from peers, resulting in reduced urgency to seek medical evaluation in acute settings. Consequently, even in the presence of significant symptoms, individuals may forgo or delay seeking emergency care, believing that social advice and informal assistance are adequate to address their health needs.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_motivation', 'spurious_motivation': 'A higher Willingness of social network may lead to lower Acute care demand leading to an ED visit because individuals embedded in supportive networks are likely to perceive their health issues as less severe due to reassurance from peers, resulting in reduced urgency to seek medical evaluation in acute settings. Consequently, even in the presence of significant symptoms, individuals may forgo or delay seeking emergency care, believing that social advice and informal assistance are adequate to address their health needs.', 'perplexity': 1.2559562464390734, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8480075671431315, 'corruption_type': 'motivation', 'min_prob': 0.13163914005869373, 'token_prob_slope': -0.002851004987957596, 'prob_variance': 0.053627841650694646, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.9448517270164112, 'avg_nll': 0.22789723180155166}

